Subject: [PATCH 26/51] tei-v7 struct-29: Require test-failure triage before
 editing: classify failure

---
 codemonkeys/prompts/editing_state_machine_prompts.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/codemonkeys/prompts/editing_state_machine_prompts.py b/codemonkeys/prompts/editing_state_machine_prompts.py
index af85cb4..6225c77 100644
--- a/codemonkeys/prompts/editing_state_machine_prompts.py
+++ b/codemonkeys/prompts/editing_state_machine_prompts.py
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ Before final approval, enumerate every caller, subclass, override, serializer, p
 
 When comparing alternative patches, first create a table with one row per issue requirement and one column per candidate. For each cell, cite the specific changed code and test result that supports or contradicts the requirement; mark missing evidence as unsupported rather than inferring support from unrelated passing tests. Reject any candidate with an unsupported requirement, a newly failing existing test, unexplained test failures, or unrelated edits. Only after all requirements are supported should test counts, patch size, and model preference break ties; prefer the smallest behaviorally complete candidate.
 
-For every requested behavior, add at least one ordinary-case check, one boundary or malformed-input check, and one regression check for previously supported behavior. If a test passes without exercising the changed branch, replace it with a more targeted check before approving the patch.
+For every requested behavior, add at least one ordinary-case check, one boundary or malformed-input check, and one regression check for previously failing behavior. After execution, classify every failure as patch-caused, pre-existing, environmental, or insufficiently exercised; cite the command and observed output for the classification. Patch-caused failures require a code revision, environmental failures require a reproducible rerun or explicit isolation, and insufficiently exercised behavior requires a new focused test before approval.iously supported behavior. If a test passes without exercising the changed branch, replace it with a more targeted check before approving the patch.
 
 Before editing, convert the issue into explicit acceptance contracts. For each contract, state the observable input, expected output, affected symbol, invariant, compatibility requirement, and a concrete validation command. Treat every contract as mandatory: do not finalize a patch until each one has an implementation rationale and a passing validation result.
 
